  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JPD 2026-2028 - Junior Secondment - JPD programme 2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">JPD 2026-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen bidrar till m&#xe5;luppfyllelsen inom strategin f&#xf6;r innovation, partnerskap och kapacitetsutveckling genom placering av svensk personal p&#xe5; internationella organisationer.

Genom programmet Junior Professionals in Delegation placeras svenska JPDs p&#xe5; delegationer f&#xf6;r att bidra till EEAS eller Europeiska Kommissionens verksamhet.

Insatsen g&#xe4;ller finansiering av sju (7) svenska traineer till EU:s traineeprogram Junior Professionals in Delegation under perioden 2026-2028. I till&#xe4;gg till de sju traineer som finansieras av Sida kommer ytterligare tv&#xe5; svenska traineer att delta i programmet under samma period. Dessa tv&#xe5; finansieras av EEAS och Europeiska Kommissionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this contribution is to provide Swedish staff within international organisations. 

The contribution is in accordance with the strategy for innovation, partnership and capacity development, providing human resources to work with and through the diverse mandates of EU Delegations. For this purpose, Sweden closely collaborates with the EEAS regarding placements in EEAS and European Commission delegations around the world through the Junior Professionals in Delegation program (JPD). Through the program, 9 Swedish JPD&apos;s will be placed at EU delegations to contribute to the EEAS and EC activities.

The contribution regards the financing of seven (7) Swedish trainees to the EU trainee programme Junior Professionals in Delegation during 2026-2028. In addition to the seven trainees financed by Sida another two Swedish trainees will, financed by the European Union External Action (EEAS) and the European Commission, participate in the program.

JPD:s are often viewed as a regular staff member and are, as such, expected to contribute to regular operations. For EC JPD:s this may entail program implementation, while for EEAS JPD:s focus is mainly on political/press function. A JPD may work with all thematic areas that the delegation operates within.</narrative>
  </description>
